{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmBoundary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmBoundary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmDeriv","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.AlternatingZetaTwo"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_eq_cLiTwo_of_norm_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_eq_cLiTwo_of_norm_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmBoundary.lean#L68-L86","doc":"**Agreement extends to the closed disc, off the cut.**\n\n`cLiTwoExt_eq_cLiTwo` gives the open disc; this reaches every boundary point\nthat is not on `[1,∞)`. Both sides are continuous there — `cLiTwo` by the\nM-test above, `cLiTwoExt` because it is analytic on `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` — and they agree\non the open disc, whose closure contains the point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousOn_cLiTwo_closedBall","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousOn_cLiTwo_closedBall","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmBoundary.lean#L49-L66","doc":"**`cLiTwo` is continuous on the closed unit disc.** Weierstrass M-test with\n`1/(k+1)²`; this is the only place the boundary is touched. ","signatureChunk":0}]}